Now I have enough understanding of the codebase. Let me create a comprehensive implementation plan for the `entire insights` command.

# Implementation Plan: `entire insights` Command

## Overview

The `entire insights` command provides analytics over session data, aggregating metrics like time spent, tokens used, files modified, and tool usage patterns. This implementation leverages existing abstractions (strategy.ListSessions, checkpoint.GitStore) and follows patterns from the explain command.

## 1. Package Structure

### Primary Files (create in `cmd/entire/cli/`)

**`insights.go`** - Main command implementation
- Command definition and flag parsing
- Routing to appropriate handlers (terminal view vs export)
- Flag validation (mutually exclusive flags, dependencies)
- Integration with checkDisabledGuard()

**`insights_analytics.go`** - Analytics computation
- SessionAnalytics aggregation
- Parallel transcript parsing with goroutines
- Tool usage extraction from transcripts
- Hourly activity bucketing

**`insights_formatters.go`** - Output formatters
- Terminal formatter (table-based with alignment)
- JSON formatter (structured export)
- Markdown formatter (documentation-ready output)

**`insights_filters.go`** - Filtering logic
- Period filtering (week/month/year based on time.Time ranges)
- Repo filtering (extract repo name from git remotes)
- Agent filtering (by agent.AgentType)

**`insights_test.go`** - Unit tests
- Analytics computation tests
- Filter logic tests
- Formatter tests (snapshot-based)
- Follows t.Parallel() pattern

**`integration_test/insights_test.go`** - Integration tests
- End-to-end command execution
- Export format validation
- Multi-session aggregation

## 2. Core Data Types

### InsightsQuery (in `insights_analytics.go`)
```go
// InsightsQuery defines filters for insights aggregation
type InsightsQuery struct {
    // Period filters sessions by time range
    Period PeriodFilter // week, month, year

    // StartTime is the inclusive start of the time window
    StartTime time.Time

    // EndTime is the exclusive end of the time window
    EndTime time.Time

    // RepoFilter limits to specific repository (extracted from git remote)
    RepoFilter string

    // AgentFilter limits to specific agent type
    AgentFilter agent.AgentType
}

// PeriodFilter represents time-based filtering
type PeriodFilter string

const (
    PeriodWeek  PeriodFilter = "week"
    PeriodMonth PeriodFilter = "month"
    PeriodYear  PeriodFilter = "year"
)
```

### InsightsReport (in `insights_analytics.go`)
```go
// InsightsReport contains aggregated analytics
type InsightsReport struct {
    // Query that generated this report
    Query InsightsQuery

    // Metadata
    GeneratedAt time.Time
    RepoName    string // Extracted from git remote

    // Aggregate Metrics
    TotalSessions       int
    TotalCheckpoints    int
    TotalTimeSeconds    int64 // Sum of session durations
    TotalTokens         int64
    EstimatedCostUSD    float64 // Based on token pricing
    AvgSessionSeconds   int64
    LongestSessionSecs  int64
    FilesModified       int // Unique files across all sessions
    CommitsLinked       int // Commits with Entire-Checkpoint trailer

    // Agent Breakdown
    AgentStats []AgentStat // Sessions/checkpoints/tokens per agent

    // Activity Patterns
    DailyActivity  []ActivityPoint // Sessions and hours per day
    WeeklyActivity []ActivityPoint // Weekly aggregates
    MonthlyActivity []ActivityPoint // Monthly aggregates

    // Top-K Lists
    TopRepos []RepoStat    // Top 5 repos by hours spent
    TopTools []ToolUsage   // Top 5 tools by invocation count

    // Recent Sessions
    RecentSessions []SessionSummary // Last 5 sessions

    // Peak Hours Heatmap (24-hour buckets, 0-23)
    PeakHours [24]int // Session count per hour of day
}

// AgentStat tracks metrics per agent
type AgentStat struct {
    Agent      agent.AgentType
    Sessions   int
    Checkpoints int
    Tokens     int64
    Percentage float64 // Percentage of total sessions
}

// ActivityPoint represents activity at a specific time
type ActivityPoint struct {
    Date     time.Time // Truncated to day/week/month
    Sessions int
    Hours    float64
}

// RepoStat tracks time spent per repository
type RepoStat struct {
    RepoName string
    Hours    float64
    Sessions int
}

// ToolUsage tracks tool invocation counts
type ToolUsage struct {
    ToolName string
    Count    int
}

// SessionSummary contains summary info for recent sessions list
type SessionSummary struct {
    SessionID   string
    StartTime   time.Time
    Duration    time.Duration
    Checkpoints int
    Description string // First prompt or derived from commits
}
```

## 3. Aggregation Logic

### Two-Tier Approach (in `insights_analytics.go`)

**Tier 1: Metadata-Rich (Fast)**
```go
// computeMetadataMetrics aggregates stats from session metadata
// Does NOT require transcript parsing
func computeMetadataMetrics(sessions []strategy.Session, store *checkpoint.GitStore) MetadataMetrics {
